# ── Zenith analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local for local dev. Both values below are PUBLIC by design:
# they ship inside the tracking snippet on every page, and the site key can
# only WRITE events. There is nothing here worth hiding.
#
# BOTH MUST BE BUILD ARGS in Docker, not just runtime env. A prerendered page
# reads them at build time; set only at runtime, the tracker never appears in
# the HTML no matter what the container environment says.
ZENITH_URL=https://analytics.gritframework.dev
ZENITH_SITE_KEY=zk_o84KgGIkU3QNkH4bC4pURnxsoeFwbmq3OfL1PeIowr4

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime env in Docker, NOT build args. None is required for tracking, and the
# site works with all three missing: /zenith answers 503 and the install-count
# badges stay hidden rather than showing zeros.
#
# ZENITH_API_KEY reads analytics. It powers both the /zenith dashboard and the
# install-count badges (GET /api/stats/events?name=block_copy). It may also be
# passed as a build arg to bake the counts into the first prerender; without it
# the numbers appear on the first ISR revalidation instead.
# ZENITH_API_KEY=
#
# The dashboard gate. Generate the hash with Zenith's own CLI, never store the
# plaintext password here.
# ZENITH_PW_HASH=
# ZENITH_JWT_SECRET=
